# Push notification backend (DIC-390)

# Vercel KV / Upstash Redis — stores push tokens, watchlists, and per-card
# alert cooldown timestamps. Replaces the old GitHub-committed JSON files so
# tokens never land in git history.
KV_REST_API_URL=
KV_REST_API_TOKEN=

# Shared secret guarding POST /api/push/notify. The endpoint is server-to-server
# only (cron / Vercel cron) and rejects every request when this is unset.
# Set the SAME value on Vercel (the API) and in the local scraper's environment.
PUSH_NOTIFY_SECRET=

# Optional override for where the scraper sends alerts (defaults to prod).
# PUSH_NOTIFY_URL=https://holocard-hunter.vercel.app/api/push/notify

# Google OAuth — REQUIRED for Google login to work (web + native).
# Missing on Vercel/EAS is what produced "Missing client ID for google" on device
# (DIC-824). authService selects the client id by Platform.OS
# (src/services/googleClientConfig.ts): iOS -> IOS id, Android -> ANDROID id,
# web -> WEB id; native falls back to generic/web only for dev. Google issues a
# SEPARATE client per app type — the web client only accepts https redirects, so a
# native build MUST use its own client id (custom-scheme redirect) or OAuth fails.
# Set the WEB id on Vercel (web build) and the IOS/ANDROID ids on EAS (native build).
# These are public client ids (safe to ship in the bundle), not secrets — but still
# set them via the platform env, not git.
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-google-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=your-web-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID=your-ios-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_ANDROID_CLIENT_ID=your-android-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com

# Apple Sign-In — backend-only secrets (set on Vercel, NEVER commit). These power
# /api/auth/apple/* (refresh_token exchange + account-deletion revoke). Client-side
# Apple login stays disabled until server-side ID-token verification ships, so the
# login screen shows an "即將開放" state instead of a failing button (DIC-824).
# See docs/AUTH_SETUP.md for how to generate the .p8 key, Key ID, and Team ID.
# APPLE_TEAM_ID=
# APPLE_CLIENT_ID=
# APPLE_KEY_ID=
# APPLE_PRIVATE_KEY=
# Optional web-only Apple client id (Services ID) consumed by the RN client once
# Apple login is re-enabled:
# EXPO_PUBLIC_APPLE_SERVICE_ID=
